I opened [Orb-agent/micro-intent#3](https://github.com/Orb-agent/micro-intent/pull/3): `feature/wp2-backend-voice-vision` into `develop`. It contains:
- the backend scaffold;
- the WebSocket server with the stub agent;
- Gradium speech in and out;
- interruption;
- the fake app for testing;
- the `AGENTS.md` team rules;
- the Gradium skills.

The description says the team is converging on the SwiftUI app with A2UI, Gradium and the WebSocket backend, not the Chrome extension. The repo has no CI set up, so the PR shows no checks. The 6 backend tests pass locally.

The three subagents (vision, screenshot upload, hands-free) are still running. As each one finishes I'll review it, merge it into this branch and push, so it lands in the same PR.

BC's and Coral's branches stay as they are. Someone should tell them about the decision. BC's agent code (`agent.py`, `sbb.py`, `calendar_source.py`) could be ported into WP3 behind the `Agent.turn()` interface. It shouldn't be merged as a separate backend.

